FindProof -- equational theorem prover (CASC UEQ entry, with a
FOF/clausal front end).

BUILD
  make                 # produces bin/FindProof  (needs a C11 compiler + libm)
  ./starexec_build     # equivalent, for StarExec

The whole engine is one self-contained translation unit; no external
dependencies beyond the C standard library and libm.

STAREXEC CONFIGURATION
  bin/starexec_run_default PROBLEM.p
      CASC proving.  Reads the wall-clock limit from
      $STAREXEC_WALLCLOCK_LIMIT (default 120s), pins
      THVM_ATP_SCHED_MAX_PAR to the node's core count, and runs a
      CONCURRENT portfolio of configuration slices, each with the full
      wall; the first proof wins.  Writes an SZS status line plus, on
      success, an SZS CNFRefutation (stdout is quiet otherwise;
      --verbose restores engine chatter).

RUN (manual)
  bin/FindProof --schedule --szs --proof --wall=120 PROBLEM.p   # portfolio
  bin/FindProof --szs PROBLEM.p                                 # single config
  bin/FindProof --check --szs PROOF.p                           # verify a proof
  bin/FindProof --list-knobs                                    # strategy surface
  bin/FindProof --list-lanes                                    # schedule lanes: name TAB flags
  bin/FindProof --lane=twee --szs --wall=120 PROBLEM.p          # one lane alone

INPUT   TPTP CNF unit-equality problems; FOF (and non-unit CNF) is
        clausified and equationalized by the built-in front end.
        include('Axioms/*.ax') directives resolve against the problem
        directory and $TPTP.
OUTPUT  SZS status (Unsatisfiable / Satisfiable / GaveUp / ResourceOut /
        Timeout; Theorem for fof conjectures) and, with --proof, an SZS
        refutation with full inference provenance.

The companion ProoVer entry, CheckProof (a first-order TSTP proof
checker built from the same sources), ships as its own tarball; see
tools/proover/ in the source repository.
